Description: Scoped network/log load-generation tool for red-team/blue-team exercises
 thugsflooder generates sustained, high-volume synthetic network traffic
 (UDP/TCP/HTTP junk and replayed traffic recordings) against an explicit,
 user-supplied allowlist of hosts/ports/protocols, with a live terminal
 dashboard (bandwidth graph, log pane, summary stats).
 .
 It will never send traffic to a target outside the allowlist, and it
 always writes a permanent audit log of every attempt. It will not run
 in any capacity without --i-understand-the-risk. Only use it against
 networks and hosts you own or are explicitly authorized to test.
